# 📈 Stock Market Time-Series Analysis (US & India)

AI-based forecasting system comparing traditional econometric models (ARIMA) with deep learning models (LSTM) for stock market prediction.

---

## 🚀 Overview

This project analyzes and forecasts stock market trends for:

- 🇺🇸 S&P 500 (US Market)
- 🇮🇳 NIFTY 50 (Indian Market)

It focuses on comparing:
- Statistical models (ARIMA)
- Deep Learning models (LSTM)

to understand which performs better in capturing market patterns.

---

## 🎯 Problem Statement

Stock market prediction is complex due to noise and volatility.  
Traditional models like ARIMA often fail to capture long-term dependencies.

This project explores whether LSTM models can improve prediction accuracy over classical approaches.

---

## 🧠 Approach

### 1. Data Collection
- Historical stock data (S&P 500, NIFTY 50)

### 2. Data Preprocessing
- Handling missing values  
- Normalization  
- Time-series formatting  

### 3. Models Implemented

#### 🔹 ARIMA
- Baseline statistical model  
- Used for time-series forecasting  

#### 🔹 LSTM (Deep Learning)
- Captures sequential dependencies  
- Designed for better long-term trend prediction  

---

## 📊 Results

- LSTM showed improved performance over ARIMA in capturing trends  
- Better handling of non-linear patterns  
- More accurate forecasting in volatile conditions  

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- Python  
- NumPy, Pandas  
- TensorFlow / Keras  
- ARIMA (statsmodels)  

---

## 📌 Key Learnings

- Deep learning models outperform traditional methods in complex datasets  
- Financial data is highly noisy and difficult to model  
- Model evaluation is as important as model building  

---

## 🚧 Future Improvements

- Add Buy/Sell signal generation  
- Integrate real-time stock data API  
- Build interactive dashboard (Streamlit)  
- Add news sentiment analysis  

